					<title>Increase data transparency</title>
				</business-objective-ref>
				<business-objective-ref Ref="0E946F0D85A5474AB07FE701864D9108" ID="7C79132C9A25427BAFC1CA3EED8E9759" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Improve inventory visibility" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="9B2167820BEE473CA0B652044612572D">
					<title>Improve inventory visibility</title>
				</business-objective-ref>
				<short-description>This scenario supports used vehicle management with a holistic and
flexible approach to manage vehicle trade-in processes as well
as vehicle sales processes. The trade-in can already start with the
sales of the new vehicle when buy-back conditions such as the
planned return date and price can be defined. Once a vehicle is
actually returned its residual value is determined which can be
done on a calculation sheet or using an external  evaluation
service. After the vehicle has been serviced for resale it can be
made visible to the entire dealer community and sold in a
locate-to-order scenario.</short-description>
				<hyperlink ID="B9C0A4DB93F44D9B8DFE344FAC8E9C84" href="https://websmp230.sap-ag.de/sap(bD1kZSZjPTAwMSZkPW1pbg==)/support/scl/default.htm?showheader=X&amp;startpage=-&amp;pstype=2&amp;psobj=01200615329100004031" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Scenario and Process Component List" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="BF5280B423D74D5E8D76596CC8C2FF64">
					<title>Scenario and Process Component List</title>
				</hyperlink>
			</business-scenario>
		</folder>
	</scenario-group>
	<scenario-group ID="88C55704D684491F9D96C1811B0ACE3F" integrated-with-supplier="true" integrated-with-consumer="true" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Service Parts Management" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="D9DC5BD8C5F84CF09486D6275CDA4CAE">
		<title>Service Parts Management</title>
		<short-description>On the one hand service parts management is a business which
delivers much better profit margins than selling vehicles. On the
other hand it is a logistical nightmare characterized by very high
numbers of stock keeping units (SKUs), high volumes of orders with
very few pieces per line item, daily varying demand, highly
frequent engineering changes and so on. As service parts
availaility and prices have a tremendous impact on customer
satisfaction the challenge is to keep service levels high while
keeping inventory levels to a minimum.   </short-description>
		<business-scenario ID="5D00A15CC4A44D638777F371E4F92C5F" bprid="30C5C89EC2B84424B2873BED865C904F" responsibleOrgUnit="PMD" xmlns:smc="http://www.sap.com/ns/smc" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Service Parts Planning" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="262C9AB434174B12B273E6077BBA5740">
			<title>Service Parts Planning</title>
			<process ID="466DBE8EFDA4401B999EAAB4A9445B48" bprrefid="" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Strategic SC Design" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="A23340CD6073495EA164B9EB45131F68">
				<sap-cover>1</sap-cover>
				<partner-cover>4</partner-cover>
				<title>Strategic SC Design</title>
				<short-description>Strategic supply chain design includes the definition of all elements of the supply chain and the corresponding monitoring. This is supported by flexible alert monitoring.</short-description>
				<process-ref icon="process-ref.gif" ID="4CFC605C0AAC43BEAF8836840C60260A" Ref="BDDF77BB4CB841F1BABAE66148E32D1C" variantOf="AAB7AD40699D4E36B8A2FA390AAEC2E0" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Strategic SC Design" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="22FC49C8952A40F6B7852F2618E97E0E">
					<title>Strategic SC Design</title>
				</process-ref>
				<product-ref Ref="D038B826DE1F48B182EE921DA3ABFE40" ID="8F2E85BDB1BA49A780D591BC3B0D6B1A" type="SAP" key="SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="0668A7324EAA46348BB56EA7F58E2EC4">
					<title>SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive</title>
				</product-ref>
			</process>
			<process ID="9BD3184AF44A49E0997D2CB8EF8AC085" bprid="67237A90865911D912D100306E055DA7" variantOf="67237A90865911D912D100306E055DA7" best-practice-available="false" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Parts Demand Planning" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="1A21E25D298A4A228DC9C40A6752B090">
				<sap-cover>1</sap-cover>
				<title>Parts Demand Planning</title>
				<bpr-element-ref ID="948A31FE06B549A18D4103F01BAEF027" elementname="BusinessProcess" Ref="urn:bprid#67237A90865911D912D100306E055DA7" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Parts Demand Planning" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="EBA3BB2F04D64BDF9874F391B90D784D">
					<title>Parts Demand Planning</title>
				</bpr-element-ref>
				<process-ref ID="4FF0B499A2A94D2BA514E6FD5B86FC91" Ref="979F16D0865811D912D100306E055DA7" variantOf="67237A90865911D912D100306E055DA7" icon="technical-variant-ref.gif" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Parts Forecasting" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="58D1BD1FC3E44B848F2AA6FD6DB7B756">
					<title>Parts Forecasting</title>
				</process-ref>
				<short-description>
					<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">Parts demand forecasting processes use flexible interactive
planning possibilities to allow organizations to create demand
plans with any level of detail. Different forecasting algorithms
and flexible macros carry out any kind of calculation or check, and
promotion planning and collaboration capabilities aid strategy
development.</p>
				</short-description>
				<product-ref Ref="D038B826DE1F48B182EE921DA3ABFE40" ID="C614953929C5493B8E973E6268A8434A" type="SAP" key="SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="137C1A2840B24EB88BC5867AF17C6D44">
					<title>SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive</title>
				</product-ref>
				<product-ref Ref="999E64EA02ED4FD18A0BD49DFC180254" ID="AD5ADEA0CCEC4695AFBC82BF16E53F63" type="SAP" key="S12" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="A0D54EDD3EBD43088321F193B6E1C6D1">
					<title>SAP ERP</title>
				</product-ref>
			</process>
			<process ID="B853D3712CCD415AAB73E78EF9D963EE" bprrefid="" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Parts Inventory Planning" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="CD9905F7CE30408B8E3EF869EDA7B235">
				<sap-cover>1</sap-cover>
				<title>Parts Inventory Planning</title>
				<process-ref icon="technical-variant-ref.gif" ID="E4AAAEC72E644C3FAAB6132E6DB94C5D" variantOf="93D66AF0810611D912D100306E055DA7" Ref="52F22200810511D912D100306E055DA7" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Safety Stock Calculation" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="4B62B6AC9F104C768502637A7EE11915">
					<title>Safety Stock Calculation</title>
				</process-ref>
				<short-description>
					<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">Safety stock is the quantity of additional stock procured and/or
held to satisfy unexpectedly high fluctuation in demand. Safety
stock planning allows organizations to meet a target service level
while creating a minimum necessary amount of safety stock
throughout the entire supply chain for all intermediate and
finished products at their respective locations.</p>
				</short-description>
				<product-ref Ref="D038B826DE1F48B182EE921DA3ABFE40" ID="96F96C616B584BBD96AAFCE068502E03" type="SAP" key="SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="C0AB8AE04866488EB5DEC046EA19B702">
					<title>SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive</title>
				</product-ref>
				<product-ref Ref="999E64EA02ED4FD18A0BD49DFC180254" ID="099EBA5A9B4748C589A099D5C37304B4" type="SAP" key="S12" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="5E959350A9AE4B478A9458F6D2C88C83">
					<title>SAP ERP</title>
				</product-ref>
			</process>
			<process ID="814F6B48E8A745C39B4381A7DE04BEC3" bprid="72072560810911D912D100306E055DA7" variantOf="72072560810911D912D100306E055DA7" best-practice-available="false" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Parts Supply Planning" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="3821571B84054E28A000D3F79E6FED34">
				<sap-cover>1</sap-cover>
				<title>Parts Supply Planning</title>
				<bpr-element-ref ID="9AC5CE676D1543ED902EEDAF2EC75F82" elementname="BusinessProcess" Ref="urn:bprid#72072560810911D912D100306E055DA7" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Parts Supply Planning" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="5380FE09E23449ACAA8EBFAF51FAA470">
					<title>Parts Supply Planning</title>
				</bpr-element-ref>
				<process-ref ID="8225A0D26B2141E0B0DCBC0E23EF32B6" Ref="824E20A0810811D912D100306E055DA7" variantOf="72072560810911D912D100306E055DA7" icon="technical-variant-ref.gif" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Distribution Requirements Planning" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="4ACBBFC14D734E3897CB2C4DF349FF57">
					<title>Distribution Requirements Planning</title>
				</process-ref>
				<short-description>
					<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">Parts supply planning integrates purchasing, production,
distribution (of demands), and transportation so that comprehensive
mid-term to long-term tactical planning and sourcing decisions can
be simulated and performed on the basis of a single, global,
consistent model.</p>
				</short-description>
				<product-ref Ref="D038B826DE1F48B182EE921DA3ABFE40" ID="077BBBB04C734D5B8BF8A2F2FB4C3649" type="SAP" key="SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="5C34F2243987456397CBE35F68B9DD08">
					<title>SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive</title>
				</product-ref>
				<product-ref Ref="999E64EA02ED4FD18A0BD49DFC180254" ID="4B40A55701F444209DD346CDA234E3FF" type="SAP" key="S12" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="B5071697A9164784BDA395B685DDBE43">
					<title>SAP ERP</title>
				</product-ref>
			</process>
			<process ID="D1C4EA9DBD6E4C739589EA949DB2A7DB" bprid="EE825030819811D912D100306E055DA7" variantOf="EE825030819811D912D100306E055DA7" best-practice-available="false" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Parts Distribution Planning" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="CC69147737114FB4B8AD4984A58A4836">
				<sap-cover>1</sap-cover>
				<title>Parts Distribution Planning</title>
				<bpr-element-ref ID="9BBD8453A453427788AE868CD9BFA49C" elementname="BusinessProcess" Ref="urn:bprid#EE825030819811D912D100306E055DA7" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Parts Distribution Planning" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="8C37AF99A8554DF09730F8B0B1EE8BD9">
					<title>Parts Distribution Planning</title>
				</bpr-element-ref>
				<process-ref ID="2B99F96E671847DB83521B0963856E32" Ref="637DA110819811D912D100306E055DA7" variantOf="EE825030819811D912D100306E055DA7" icon="technical-variant-ref.gif" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Inventory Balancing" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="8798C6B564074CFBA695F7FF19ECA94F">
					<title>Inventory Balancing</title>
				</process-ref>
				<process-ref ID="0BE422877A0D4F9E8712B77FA546E14D" Ref="C27E1D30819711D912D100306E055DA7" variantOf="EE825030819811D912D100306E055DA7" icon="technical-variant-ref.gif" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Pull Deployment" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="8D32BFEF6CD346CAB061474A6D4895AF">
					<title>Pull Deployment</title>
				</process-ref>
				<short-description>
					<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">The parts distribution planning process is used to determine
which demands can be fulfilled by existing supply elements.</p>
				</short-description>
				<product-ref Ref="D038B826DE1F48B182EE921DA3ABFE40" ID="96158BFCC603402D9539EEFB95B85DC2" type="SAP" key="SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="B8091208F94D406889FE53C9E733BDC0">
					<title>SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive</title>
				</product-ref>
				<product-ref Ref="999E64EA02ED4FD18A0BD49DFC180254" ID="6BDE927B8A04428A8F1CAAA540082694" type="SAP" key="S12" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="137F558C2266480EB550C3DDAF246CCA">
					<title>SAP ERP</title>
				</product-ref>
			</process>
			<process ID="E333FFCE034341B8B74CBDCCB63D27A4" bprrefid="" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Supplier Collaboration" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="FF42B2ED7F7B459C90DD0184081991BA">
				<sap-cover>1</sap-cover>
				<title>Supplier Collaboration</title>
				<short-description>Supplier Managed Inventory Processing is a replenishment process were the Supplier assumes responsibility of the replenishment planning and execution, instead of the Customer (or Customer's ERP/MRP system). The Supplier recieves updates on gross demand (dependent requirements) and stock in SAP ICH, and uses min/max stock level logic to calculate a suitable replenishment plan, and consequently creates PO's and ASNs to indicate plan commitment and shipments, which updates the Customer's ERP system accordingly.</short-description>
				<process-ref icon="technical-variant-ref.gif" ID="2A243D5EDF2945F0ABE71893AE63BDC9" variantOf="F9F16A1F82464362AAC54C20199A430B" Ref="9D52284054BDEC04E10000000A114AB6" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Supplier Managed Inventory Processing" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="ADC2D1A2844A4EEF9B2BEA211EFCDC47">
					<title>Supplier Managed Inventory Processing</title>
				</process-ref>
				<product-ref Ref="D038B826DE1F48B182EE921DA3ABFE40" ID="35647EB863614B25965556C8B7B461F9" type="SAP" key="SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="A4A220B60A0D41288A74DD81CB5E8782">
					<title>SAP Service Parts Planning for Automotive</title>
				</product-ref>
			</process>
			<bpr-element-ref ID="B46CB36EC4FA4AFE8BB06946864A6818" elementname="Scenario" Ref="urn:bprid#30C5C89EC2B84424B2873BED865C904F" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Service Parts Planning" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="10035E5A81FE43638B4ACB364246565C">
				<title>Service Parts Planning</title>
			</bpr-element-ref>
			<process ID="6A5E298662DD4988BB193C7FAD80FCF1" bprid="A6744FEB84BC45B0BBDF5D75BA240463" variantOf="575BAFDDF9A54E6DB3CCB151C112811F" best-practice-available="false" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Supply Chain Monitoring and Control" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="F03735567E034EABB08955B459BF31AF">
				<title>Supply Chain Monitoring and Control</title>
				<short-description>Supply Chain Performance Management (SCPM) enables you to define, select, and monitor key performance indicators (KPIs), giving you an integrated, comprehensive view of performance across the supply chain. SCPM with mySAP SCM includes a large number of predefined KPIs based on the Supply Chain Operations Reference model (SCOR) covering all supply chain activities including source, plan, make, deliver, and return.</short-description>
				<bpr-element-ref ID="424C93C170DA4AE4B6924CA7AA358601" elementname="BusinessProcess" Ref="urn:bprid#A6744FEB84BC45B0BBDF5D75BA240463" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Supply Chain Monitoring and Control" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="03F6F833DEBC4F4D9FB134AB7DA417AF">
					<title>Supply Chain Monitoring and Control</title>
				</bpr-element-ref>
				<sap-cover>1</sap-cover>
				<process-ref Ref="A6744FEB84BC45B0BBDF5D75BA240463" ID="7739154E783143D8BC350142B7A00BD3" variantOf="575BAFDDF9A54E6DB3CCB151C112811F" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Supply Chain Monitoring and Control" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="5977969A0CE3480B93CFDBD1F36721FE">
					<title>Supply Chain Monitoring and Control</title>
				</process-ref>
				<process-ref Ref="6A5E298662DD4988BB193C7FAD80FCF1" ID="DBD37350E8D94DFC8DE57671CD517A4D" variantOf="575BAFDDF9A54E6DB3CCB151C112811F" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Supply Chain Monitoring and Control" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="E44914E08D834EF48BCE491CF278C740">
					<title>Supply Chain Monitoring and Control</title>
				</process-ref>
