						<title>Local Payments with In-House Cash</title>
					</process-ref>
					<product-ref Ref="999E64EA02ED4FD18A0BD49DFC180254" ID="3CB2B8BB3EAA446DB5F97369DE2B453A" type="SAP" key="S12" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="42A1A9A8C1164C0D9D47686B0A367B69">
						<title>SAP ERP</title>
					</product-ref>
					<process-ref Ref="CB5270B023A311DA12D100306E055DA7" ID="E207FB18337948EE8546F695E633D5BB" variantOf="87D450C023A711DA12D100306E055DA7" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Central Incoming Payments with In-House Cash" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="F57DB5DA328B4D3EB5C18CB49881C37F">
						<title>Central Incoming Payments with In-House Cash</title>
					</process-ref>
					<content>
						<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"> </p>
					</content>
					<product-ref Ref="5CE3CF2EC8F1431F8BF94EB3FE33B368" ID="16CD28D6BA92406DAEBCFC485CA9F268" type="SAP" key="SAP FSCM II (Placeholder ERP Map only)" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP: Treasury - SAP Treasury and Risk Management" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="D6F41A5319014F008445E8DCF43C2ED2">
						<title>SAP ERP: Treasury - SAP Treasury and Risk Management</title>
					</product-ref>
					<product-ref Ref="2130EAF869E44EC19E6FD4733971D1E3" ID="599B3FE30FDE4E4FB78A3B7217F7B190" type="SAP" key="SAP ERP: SAP Financial Supply Chain Management - Bank Relationship Management" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP: Treasury - SAP Bank Communication Management" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="15A09D3D4A4C41F28A7620A5309AABE0">
						<title>SAP ERP: Treasury - SAP Bank Communication Management</title>
					</product-ref>
					<short-description>
						<p style="CLEAR: none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
         The SAP In-House Cash application allows
diversified companies to optimize their intra-group payment
transactions by opening an in-house bank. An In-House Cash Center
is a virtual bank within the corporate group, with which each
associated company has one account or more. For the associated
companies, the In-House Cash Center is just another house bank,
which they use primarily to process payables and receivables
involving other group companies. At the same time, you can set up
accounts for external companies that are not associated with the
group. This allows them to be included in the netting
process.
         <br></br>
         The In-House Cash Center is used to process all payments between
company units, thus keeping cash resources within the group and
optimizing how they are applied. This saves on the costs of
external netting services and gives you greater flexibility when
you process payment netting transactions.
         <br></br>
         The SAP In-House Cash component allows companies with a diversified
organizational structure to minimize the actual flow of cash and
therefore reduce bank charges, interest expenses and losses
resulting from delays in value-dating payments. It also helps to
avoid many of the disadvantages associated with external clearing
solutions, such as inflexible procedures with fixed dates and extra
costs resulting from manual post processing. By managing accounts
centrally, you can assure your company's ability to pay, optimize
credit management, minimize interest expenses, and maximize
interest revenues.
        </p>
					</short-description>
				</process>
				<process ID="F3435DFD399A49668394EF6D33F55214" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Bank Communication Management" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="DAC0CEB3684E428F90A29DC485B7ABA4">
					<title>Bank Communication Management</title>
					<sap-cover>1</sap-cover>
					<product-ref Ref="999E64EA02ED4FD18A0BD49DFC180254" ID="DCB40081AFD14C84A37DE038A7D30A55" type="SAP" key="S12" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="0A66B13DC21E457DBBE403BFE4645731">
						<title>SAP ERP</title>
					</product-ref>
					<product-ref Ref="9FD4912571AF4371917B9AEF3849D1A9" ID="2B8C0D6B4BD74332948BFD17C53EB157" type="SAP" key="SAP Integration Package for SWIFT" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP Integration Package for SWIFT" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="9F561DB250E847C1A6C236470F194CB7">
						<title>SAP Integration Package for SWIFT</title>
					</product-ref>
					<product-ref Ref="C336F251A4354DC49EB2BD25B25DC561" ID="0FE1B347B858405B91B3E553245AC4D6" type="SAP" key="S8" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP: Financial Supply Chain Management - Biller Direct, Dispute, Credit and Collections Mgmt." OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="48EB8AE866F94B75979197A29808F9E3">
						<title>SAP ERP: Financial Supply Chain Management - Biller Direct, Dispute, Credit and Collections Mgmt.</title>
					</product-ref>
					<product-ref Ref="5CE3CF2EC8F1431F8BF94EB3FE33B368" ID="66AA6C6A7DF9437CABC2AD7DBC009146" type="SAP" key="SAP ERP: SAP Financial Supply Chain Management - Treasury Management and In-House Cash" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP: Treasury - SAP Treasury and Risk Management" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="4FF81D14B9A5494E9C3494E9791399E1">
						<title>SAP ERP: Treasury - SAP Treasury and Risk Management</title>
					</product-ref>
					<process-ref Ref="CAB43C4656E1B703E10000000A114AB6" ID="B4D9538417DE4C9EA93CE0E9F2F9F0E1" icon="technical-process-variant.gif" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: Processing Outbound payments using Bank Communication Management" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="261208E3BA7241ACAB213E9629229F1E">
						<title>Processing Outbound payments using Bank Communication Management</title>
					</process-ref>
					<short-description>
						<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">SAP Bank Communication
Management is used for managing multiple bank communication
interfaces, enabling you to connect to your bank, track the entire
payment life cycle of a transaction, and improve straight-through
processing rates and internal compliance. SAP Bank Communication
Management is also responsible for the creation and approval of
batches, the payment status monitor, and the bank statement
monitor.</p>
						<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"> </p>
						<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">With SAP Bank
Communication Management, the payments in one or several payment
runs can be presented and processed in a payment statement monitor.
This monitor also serves as a repository for incoming status
messages from SWIFT and from individual banks. The payments in the
payment run can be grouped to one or several batches according to
your needs. For example, payments can be grouped according to low
value and high value payments. You can also use digital signatures
to approve, reject, or resubmit payments.</p>
						<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"> </p>
						<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">SAP Bank Communication
Management can also be used in conjunction with the SAP Integration
Package for SWIFT. This provides you with one single interface for
bank communications via SWIFTNet.</p>
					</short-description>
					<product-ref Ref="2130EAF869E44EC19E6FD4733971D1E3" ID="3A7528BF2B2148C9856F187C0596C06A" type="SAP" key="SAP ERP: SAP Financial Supply Chain Management - Bank Relationship Management" OriginalMap="Automotive - Sales &amp; Service Organizations: SAP ERP: Treasury - SAP Bank Communication Management" OriginalMapID="4737C4AEFF9E794E8ADFC17DF0FB88F8" SrcID="AD078A71B9564B14A93532CD711ED370">
						<title>SAP ERP: Treasury - SAP Bank Communication Management</title>
					</product-ref>
				</process>
